# A game whose highlight reel is up on the Sports Connection's Instagram, keyed
# by the game's YouTube id -> the reel's shortcode. Matched on 2026-10-12 by
# reading every reel's caption: each names the sport and the opponent, and the
# post date sits a day or two after the game, which together pin one game. Two
# games have both a game-highlights reel and a play-of-the-game reel. Which to
# use, as the site owner set it on 2026-10-12: prefer the game-highlights reel;
# where a game has only a play-of-the-game reel, use that. A game absent from
# here gets a greyed Highlight button. Currently 20 are game highlights and 10
# are plays of the game, each of those ten having no fuller reel on the
# account. Instagram's own blockquote
# embed would pull Meta's JavaScript onto every page that carries one; the
# /embed iframe shows the same reel and keeps that inside the frame. Tested
# 2026-10-12 in a browser with no Instagram session: it renders and plays, and
# a viewer without an account is never asked to log in.
