 '<h3 class="warrant-doc__art">ARTICLE 26<span>(Appropriation:  Fiscal Year 2026 Community '
 'Preservation Committee)</span></h3>'
 '<p>To see what sums the Town will vote to appropriate, and also to raise, borrow pursuant to '
 'any applicable statute or transfer from available funds, or reserve for later appropriation '
 'monies from the Community Preservation Fund annual revenues or available funds for the '
 'administrative and operating expenses of the Community Preservation Committee, the undertaking '
 'of Community Preservation Projects and all other necessary and proper expenses for the year; '
 'or to take any other action relative thereto.</p>'
 '<p class="warrant-doc__by">(Select Board for Community Preservation Committee) </p>'
 '<p>FINANCE COMMITTEE MOTION:  Moved that the following sums be appropriated or reserved for '
 'later appropriation from the Community Preservation Fund Fiscal Year 2026 revenues or other '
 'available funds as indicated herein, for the administrative and operating expenses of the '
 'Community Preservation Committee, the undertaking of community preservation projects and all '
 'other necessary and proper expenses, for Fiscal Year 2026 community preservation purposes as '
 'set forth herein, with each item considered a separate appropriation to be spent by the '
 'Community Preservation Committee, as shown below with any strikeouts indicating deletions from '
 'the Community Preservation Committee article and any highlighted text indicating '
 'additions/modifications:</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Purpose</td><td>'
 'Amount</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>Historic Preservation</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>St. Paul&rsquo;s '
 'Church</td><td>$957,770</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>St. Paul&rsquo;s Church has had a long and productive history of working with the Community '
 'Preservation Committee for over two decades. This is an important historic structure. This '
 'request is for funding to continue the restoration and preservation efforts by improving '
 'egress and installing HVAC and a sprinkler system.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Housing '
 'Authority/Miacomet Village</td><td>$341,030</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>This request is for restoration and preservation of the 40-year-old affordable duplex '
 'structure at 8 Benjamin Drive, with work to include replacement of cedar shingles, rotting '
 'trim, windows and doors.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Maria Mitchell '
 'Association</td><td>$145,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>This request is part of a continuing effort to preserve and restore the historic Maria '
 'Mitchell Vestal Street Observatory and Astronomical Study. This project would replace the '
 'roof.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Landmark House - '
 'Nantucket Community Service Inc. This request is for rebuilding the handicap</td><td>'
 '$149,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>ramp/stairs/retaining walls to the rear main accessible entrance to the building.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>ReMain 58 LLC</td>'
 '<td>$699,303</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>This is an application on behalf of the Folger Block Condominium Trust. This is a prominent '
 'individually significant historic structure on Main Street. It is unique due to the '
 'architecture and exterior composition of the building. It has a specific place in time that no '
 'other Nantucket structure has. This project is for exterior restoration, stormwater '
 'management, and waterproofing. Funds were dispersed in FY 2025 for a comprehensive survey of '
 'the exterior upon which this grant request was made.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Historical '
 'Association</td><td>$288,002</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>After receiving substantial CPC funding over several years to preserve and secure the Fair '
 'Street Museum, it was found that the structure had significant issues with water intrusion '
 'from the roof and skylight. This request is for replacement of the roof and skylight, '
 'relocation of the roof condensers and repair/replacement of historic fencing at the 7 Fair '
 'Street research library.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Historical '
 'Association</td><td>$134,815</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>This request for funding is for replacement of the roof, and restoration of the unique '
 'windows at Greater Light.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Town '
 'Clerk</td><td>$9,500</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>These funds are for the preservation and restoration of Civil War Veterans&rsquo; documents '
 'through digitization.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Sub-total</td><td>'
 '$2,724,420</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>All the funds to be used in this category are from the Community Preservation surcharge, '
 'interest, and the State matching funds.</p>'
 '<p>Community Housing</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Interfaith '
 'Council</td><td>$380,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>Funds for rental assistance program, housing and rental assistance to low and '
 'moderate-income Nantucket year-round working families. The CPC has worked cooperatively with '
 'the Council since 2005. The program has been very successful and assisted many Nantucket '
 'resident to be in safe, legal housing.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Affordable Housing '
 'Trust Fund</td><td>$350,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>This allocation is for the use of funds to make a payment on the first of two Five Million '
 'Dollar Bonds taken on behalf of the Affordable Housing Trust for the cost of acquiring land, '
 'which may include buildings thereon, and infrastructure, for the development of affordable '
 'housing and for the costs of designing, constructing, reconstructing and equipping affordable '
 'housing.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Sub-total</td><td>'
 '$730,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>All the funds to be used in this category are from the Community Preservation surcharge, '
 'interest and the State matching funds.</p>'
 '<p>Open Space Conservation/Recreation</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Lighthouse '
 'School</td><td>$83,950</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>This request is for the creation of a new rain garden, as part of a drainage improvement '
 'project on the property. The rain garden will be located immediately abutting the Fairgrounds '
 'Road bike path and be directly accessible by the public. Educational aspects of the rain '
 'garden will be provided on site.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Nantucket Racquet '
 'Sports Association</td><td>$316,050</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>The Association has been adding to the sports complex off of Nobadeer Farm/Hinsdale Roads '
 'over the years with approval of the Nantucket Land Bank as the complex is on its property. The '
 'CPC has funded this effort since FY 2021. This request is for the racquet sports facility '
 'expansion. Use is available at reasonable costs to all members of the community. The CPC '
 'continues to support the Association&rsquo;s efforts to provide more recreational outlets for '
 'the Community. A recreational facility that welcomes all members of the community regardless '
 'of socioeconomic status is important for physical and mental health.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Sub-total</td><td>'
 '$400,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>All the funds to be used in this category are from the Community Preservation surcharge, '
 'interest and the State matching funds.</p>'
 '<p>Administration</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Community '
 'Preservation Committee</td><td>$200,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>Administrative and operating expenses. The State Act that created CPCs requires 5% of the '
 'available funds to be set aside for administrative costs.</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Sub-total</td><td>'
 '$200,000</td></tr></table></div>'
 '<p>All the funds to be used in this category are from the Community Preservation surcharge, '
 'interest and the State matching funds.</p>'
 '<p class="warrant-doc__term">TOTAL</p>'
 '<p>All amounts to be appropriated from the following sources:</p>'
 '<p>SOURCES AMOUNT</p>'
 '<div class="warrant-doc__scroll"><table class="warrant-doc__grid"><tr><td>Raised and '
