# retyped. Two things had to survive that. The Town marks proposed bylaw edits
# by drawing rectangles rather than by styling the text -- a grey box behind
# new language, a hairline through language to be struck -- so plain text
# extraction welds the old wording to the new; "as measured by the exterior
# interior faces of the exterior walls" is one real line of it. Every
# character was tested against its own page's rectangles instead, and the
# edits come through here as <del> and <ins>. The second is shape: the bylaw
# lists hang their wrapped lines off a marker, and the compensation schedules
# are real grids. Both are columns on the page and tables here.
