# from elsewhere on the site and carry their own longer text here, the way
# "One Million Daffodils" does on the Chamber page.
#
# The second section is headed "Interview with the Executive Director", not
# "Giving bACK" -- Frank's wording, 2026-10-25. The show's name stays in the
# two video titles, and the section is still named for the show on the
# Community Foundation and Past Shows pages.

NFFRA_MISSION = (
    '<span class="dl-mission__lead">About Nantucket Food, Fuel &amp; Rental Assistance:</span>'
    "<br><br>The NFFRA is an outreach service of the Nantucket Interfaith Council. The Nantucket "
    "Interfaith Council is a group of island churches, religious organizations, and community "
    "members who meet monthly to promote the spiritual and humanitarian wellbeing of our island "
    "community. Services are provided without regard to race, sex, creed, religious belief or "
    "sexual orientation."
    '<br><br><span class="dl-mission__lead">The Nantucket Food Pantry</span><br>'
    "The food pantry was founded in 1991. We know there are still many hungry neighbors who we "
    "are not yet serving. The Food Assistance Program will continue outreach efforts to identify "
    "and meet more of the existing need. We&rsquo;re excited to announce that the Nantucket Food "
    "Pantry has moved to its new permanent home at 19 Boynton Lane! To contact the Nantucket "
    'Food Pantry please call <a href="tel:+15082287438">(508) 228-7438</a> or e-mail '
    '<a href="mailto:food@assistnantucket.org">food@assistnantucket.org</a>.'
    '<br><br><span class="dl-mission__lead">The Nantucket Rental Assistance Program</span><br>'
    "The Rental Assistance program began in 2004. The need for an island-based rental assistance "
    "program remains critical due to the following challenges: a growing year-round population "
    "living at or below the median income level; rising rental costs in relation to wages "
    "earned; a severe shortage of year-round affordable rental housing; reduced employment faced "
    "by many "
    "workers during the &ldquo;off season.&rdquo; To contact the Nantucket Rental Assistance "
    'Program please call <a href="tel:+15089011320">(508) 901-1320</a> or e-mail '
    '<a href="mailto:nffra@assistnantucket.org">nffra@assistnantucket.org</a>.'
    '<br><br><span class="dl-mission__lead">The Nantucket Fuel Assistance Program</span><br>'
    "The Fuel Assistance program was created in 2014 to assist clients apply for heat subsidies "
    "under the Federal Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program, and in 2016 with the Salvation "
    "Army Good Neighbor Energy Program. To contact the Nantucket Fuel Assistance Program please "
    'call <a href="tel:+15089011320">(508) 901-1320</a> or e-mail '
    '<a href="mailto:nffra@assistnantucket.org">nffra@assistnantucket.org</a>.')

NFFRA_PROGRAMS = [
 ("zB7sLwBJs-8", "Nantucket Food Fuel Rental Assistance Promo (2019)",
   "NCTV&rsquo;s profile of all three programs, filmed in 2019, so the figures in it are the "
   "ones that held then. Staff explain that NFFRA is a secular outreach program of the Nantucket "
   "Interfaith Council, meeting islanders who work hard against a high cost of living, a "
   "shortage of stable housing and a seasonal economy. The food pantry, thirty years old at the "
   "time, was serving about 482 families and handing out some 10,000 bags of food a year. "
   "Volunteers walk through the week: unloading the delivery truck, stocking the shelves and "
   "freezers, filling the grocery lists clients check off, bagging food rescued from restaurants "
   "and farms before it is thrown away, and driving deliveries to people who cannot get there. "
   "The fuel program, then the newest, helps residents apply for state and federal heating "
   "subsidies and sometimes pays directly to stop a midwinter shutoff. A woman who fell down a "
   "full flight of stairs while shaking out scatter rugs describes what short-term rental "
   "assistance meant on a fixed income: she was born here, she says, and wants to stay."),
 ("qdZmjVUZ5OE",
  "2023 Achievement of Merit Award &ndash; Nantucket Food, Fuel &amp; Rental Assistance",
   "The food pantry&rsquo;s manager accepts the Chamber of Commerce&rsquo;s Achievement of Merit "
   "Award and uses the time to describe the work. She begins with the misconception she meets "
   "most: that an island this wealthy would not need a food pantry. She describes handing out "
   "thousands of bags of groceries a month with no questions asked, a deliberate choice given "
   "how seasonal island employment is, and contrasts it with rental assistance, which vets "
   "applications closely and helps sixty to seventy families a month. She notes the smaller fuel "
   "and medical assistance programs, says the organization never closed a day through the "
   "pandemic, and credits the volunteers who come in daily."),
]

NFFRA_GIVING_BACK = [
 ("tPnYGf9NQts",
  "Giving bACK w/ Janis Carreiro, Executive Director for NFFRA Outreach Programs &ndash; Day One",
   "Part one of Giving bACK&rsquo;s first two-part episode. Arthur Bergeron and Sunny Daily talk "
   "to Janis Carreiro, who has run these programs since 2007, and spend most of the half hour on "
   "the food pantry. She starts with the name, which is longer than the sign suggests &mdash; "
   "food, fuel, rental assistance and medical travel, run as secular programs under the "
   "Nantucket Interfaith Council. Then the pantry&rsquo;s history: a tiny basement room at St. "
   "Paul&rsquo;s in 2007, one way in and out, pre-made bags that were ninety percent canned and "
   "shelf-stable; a move to the back of the NRTA station; and the pandemic, when it ran six days "
   "a week and shifted twice, to the White Elephant ballroom and then an elementary school "
   "cafeteria. It came out of that serving fresh fruit, vegetables and protein from island "
   "farms, restaurants and individuals, and it now reaches roughly 2,000 families &mdash; about "
   "4,000 people &mdash; with 300 coming through on a busy evening. She also explains that the "
   "pantry has to leave the space it has long rented for a dollar a year and what that will "
   "cost; at the time of this recording a new home had not been found. The last stretch turns to "
   "rental assistance, begun around 2003 by two island reverends on a small Community "
   "Preservation Committee grant and helping about ten people in its first year, and to who "
   "needs it now: seasonal and self-employed workers with no unemployment to fall back on, "
   "construction and service workers through a long cold spell, families knocked sideways by "
   "sudden illness, and a growing number of older tenants whose pensions and Social Security "
   "have not kept pace with rents."),
 ("QfU1YROPl5Y",
  "Giving bACK w/ Janis Carreiro, Executive Director for NFFRA Outreach Programs &ndash; Day Two",
   "Part two, and the half of the organization the first episode ran out of time for. After a "
   "one-minute recap &mdash; the pantry open Tuesday to Thursday afternoons, rental assistance "
   "reaching 100 to 120 families a year, paid to the landlord rather than the tenant and only "
   "after a vetting interview &mdash; Janis Carreiro turns to the two smaller programs. Utility "
   "assistance has three parts: taking over from the town the job of walking people through the "
   "state low-income energy application, administering the Salvation Army&rsquo;s one-time "
   "benefit for those who do not qualify for it, and a private trust set up in the 1890s for the "
   "widows and orphans of Nantucket, whose trustee asked NFFRA to assess applications and deal "
   "with the vendors directly. It is the least funded of the programs, reaching 40 to 50 "
   "families with one or two bills each, priority going to anyone facing a shutoff &mdash; and "
   "she explains the trick of getting a household current enough that the utility will put it on "
   "a budget plan at all. The medical travel program came out of a grant made when the new "
   "hospital was built, held and managed by the Community Foundation, and covers ferry "
   "reservations, car rentals and hospital parking for people who have to leave the island for "
   "care that is not available here. Bergeron closes on the 1890s trust as an argument for "
   "legacy giving."),
]

