NPC_HARVESTER = [
 ("https://vimeo.com/232546260", "Aquatic Harvester Thank You Celebration",
   "On 19 August 2017 at Hummock Pond, Bob Williams of the Nantucket Pond Coalition thanks the "
   "town and the Nantucket Land Bank for sponsoring the aquatic harvester, a 4,500-pound paddle "
   "wheeler that takes off about 130 cubic feet of weed a load. Left to die and decompose on the "
   "bottom, he says, that vegetation draws down a pond&rsquo;s oxygen, loads it with nutrients "
   "and turns it by degrees into a swamp. Rita Higgins, newly elected to the Board of Selectmen, "
   "calls the ponds an indicator of what development is doing to the island&rsquo;s natural "
   "systems; the two can go hand in hand, she says, but the island has to act now. The executive "
   "director of the Nantucket Islands Land Bank sets out a third year of phragmites spraying on "
   "Long Pond, the hope of extending it to all the Land Bank&rsquo;s frontage there, and "
   "loosestrife and phragmites work at Miacomet. The Nantucket Land Council describes the "
   "federal phosphorus grant it manages with the town on Long, Hummock and Miacomet, and the "
   "water quality sampling it is doing before and after this harvest. John Johnson, thirty years "
   "on Miacomet Pond, says the reeds have closed in where the water was once open, and that the "
   "children who used to swim there no longer do. A Long Pond landowner describes the fund the "
   "twenty-two abutters have opened to clear the phragmites themselves. Williams closes on the "
   "day&rsquo;s haul: some 30,000 cubic feet of weed, bound for the composter at the landfill as "
   "fertilizer.",
   "npc-harvester-party.webp"),
 ("https://vimeo.com/137899684", "Hummock Pond Harvester Demonstration",
   "An aquatic harvester demonstration at Hummock Pond on 20 August 2015. The machine works the "
   "pond under its own paddle wheels, cutting below the surface and carrying the weed up a "
   "conveyor to a waiting front loader. John Bartlett of Bartlett&rsquo;s Farm, whose loader "
   "moved the cut vegetation up the beach, Selectman Rick Atherton, and Phil Albertson of the "
   "Nantucket Anglers Club each speak to the camera with the crowd of onlookers behind them, and "
   "kayakers and paddleboarders go by on the pond. The closing credits thank Bartlett&rsquo;s "
   "Farm, the Nantucket Land Bank, Aquatic Control Technology and limnologist Ken Wagner.",
   "npc-harvester-demo.webp"),
 ("DO-TyrjrbAw", "Harvester Demonstration Reception",
   "Bob Williams speaking to the crowd at Hummock Pond, beside the pile the harvester has "
   "built. He sets out the rest of the season &mdash; a phragmites mitigation pilot on Long "
   "Pond at the end of the month, and a federal grant for a blue-green algae project on "
   "Miacomet Pond over the winter &mdash; and makes the case for the work: a pond eleven "
   "thousand years old, turned murky and swampy by a century of septic systems on sandy soil, "
   "fertilizer, household products and acid rain; three ways to answer it, of which dredging is "
   "too expensive and hydro-raking too complicated, which leaves harvesting; and a goal that is "
   "not to clear the pond of weed but to slow the human acceleration of a natural process. The "
   "machine is an HP 5-130, its five-foot reciprocating bar cutting four feet under the surface "
   "onto a conveyor. He thanks the Coalition&rsquo;s advisory board, the Land Bank, the Land "
   "Council, the Conservation Foundation, the town&rsquo;s natural resources department and the "
   "town manager, and John Bartlett, whose front loader arrived the morning after a "
   "ten-o&rsquo;clock-at-night text and who will compost the harvested weed back onto the "
   "farm&rsquo;s fields. Selectman Rick Atherton speaks for the town, and the Land "
   "Council&rsquo;s water quality specialist closes on the multi-tool approach: pond openings "
   "that flush the pond and draw clean salt water in, the harvester taking nutrients out load "
   "by load, the fertilizer regulations on the Board of Health&rsquo;s books, and septic "
   "systems pumped on a regular schedule."),
]

