# NANTUCKET ARTS COUNCIL -- the last of the Community Foundation's four
# Initiative Funds to get a page of its own. The whole channel is here:
# twelve videos, none of them already on the site.
#
# Every description is the Council's own YouTube text, at Frank's
# instruction, not a description written from the video. Converting it to
# page markup took four changes and no others, each verified by a
# word-level diff against the channel: line breaks became <br>, runs of
# spaces were collapsed, "-Painter" got its space back, "theFall" got its
# space back, and the two Merit Award and Arts Fest lines that stop without
# one got a full stop. "Nantucket Arts Festival the Fall of 2012" is left
# as published, missing "in".
#
# The Council closes all four Emergence episodes with the same paragraph
# about the series. It is set once as the section's note instead of four
# times on the cards -- Frank's call. The wording is still theirs.
#
# Titles are normalised the way the Pond Coalition's are -- the Council's
# own name comes off the front, since the page is headed by its mark, and
# the pipe organ title's unclosed quotation mark is closed.

