# Ordered by when the footage was shot, oldest first — NOT by upload date, which
# is meaningless here: 41 of these 44 went up in 2011-2012 when the NHA
# digitized the collection. The shooting date comes from the title where it has
# one ("Nantucket winter, 1964"), otherwise from the description.
#
# Don't re-sort this by scraping the earliest year out of each description: six
# entries carry dates that have nothing to do with the footage — a subject's
# birth year (Jose Reyes 1902-1980, Tony Sarg 1880-1942), background history
# (LV 112 entered service in 1936; the film is of its 1975 return), a narration
# recorded in 1991 over 1927 footage, and the 2023 exhibition one film was cut
# for. The dates were read, not scraped. Ties break on precision — a known
# month, then an exact year, then "c. 1930", then a whole decade — and then on
# title.
