  "South Road and Sparks Avenue, a change to the direction cars enter, and a larger rotary, at "
  "an estimated $5.8 million &mdash; for an intersection that ranks in the top five percent for "
  "crashes on the island. Around thirty-four weddings had been booked for the weekend of the "
  "nor&rsquo;easter, some cancelled and others replanned in a couple of days. Erosion from that "
  "same storm uncovers wreckage at Miacomet Beach that the Historical Association believes may "
  "be the Warren Sawyer, a wooden sailing ship driven ashore there in 1884 on a run from New "
  "Orleans to Boston; her crew was taken off by the Surfside Life-Saving Station, and some of "
