# A flat list, not a year dict: all seven interviews came out at once, so a year
# picker would render a single button over the whole section. Switch to the dict
# form if a second year ever appears.
#
# On YouTube all seven carry the same boilerplate paragraph about the Civic
# Engagement Initiative, which would read as seven identical cards. These were
# written from each interview instead.
CIVIC_ENGAGEMENT = [
 ("8lgAwLVU8cQ", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Pauline Proch",
  "Pauline Proch describes how the school population has shifted &mdash; from roughly 90 "
  "percent white students when she started to about half today, with nearly 40 percent of "
  "children speaking a language other than English as their first language. She argues that a "
  "school committee should reflect the community it serves, and encourages families of color "
  "and parents of younger children to run or to join school councils as parent "
  "representatives."),
 ("JoSkMfYdMQQ", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Brooke Mohr",
  "Brooke Mohr, vice chair of the Affordable Housing Trust and chair of the Council for Human "
  "Services, describes how much more readily one can affect change on Nantucket than in a "
  "larger community. Her advice for anyone curious is to start by attending public meetings and "
  "speaking during the public comment portion, then to take a back seat and listen for a while "
  "after joining a committee."),
 ("_a9tBb0ygVQ", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Maria Partida",
  "Maria Partida came to the island at nineteen and started out cleaning houses, then found "
  "herself interpreting for neighbors at the hospital, at school, and in job interviews. Asked "
  "why she volunteers so much, her answer is simply &ldquo;why not&rdquo; &mdash; and she "
  "describes the people serving on island committees as willing to help and willing to find "
  "solutions."),
 ("hgw-Btw1Z3o", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Ray Pohl",
  "Ray Pohl, an architect who moved to Nantucket in 1990, chairs the Historic District "
  "Commission after seven years on the board. He explains what the commission is actually "
  "charged with &mdash; regulating design so that new building keeps faith with the "
  "architectural traditions established in the whaling days &mdash; and corrects a common "
  "misreading of that mission as limiting growth."),
 ("UfHOZvplLys", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Denice Kronau",
  "Denice Kronau came to the Finance Committee by way of the group founded after the 2016 "
  "election to get Nantucket women engaged in civic activity. A former chief financial officer, "
  "she put together a r&eacute;sum&eacute; and petitioned each member of the Select Board for "
  "the appointment, then spent her first year mostly listening &mdash; on the principle that "
  "one of her key skills is being able to say she doesn&rsquo;t know and ask for help."),
 ("9a-RUdjTpIE", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Rita Higgins",
  "Rita Higgins first came to Nantucket as a small child, returned after university, and "
  "settled on the island full time in 2013. With a background in the environment, she describes "
  "the fine balance between the island&rsquo;s history, its architecture, and the wildness of "
  "the moors and dunes &mdash; and why, in 2017, she came to feel that balance needed someone "
  "advocating for it."),
 ("_-ZQJ22MgZM", "N. Civic League&rsquo;s Interviews about Civic Engagement: Vanessa Rendeiro",
  "Vanessa Rendeiro, a former English and Portuguese teacher from Bel&eacute;m in Brazil, has "
  "lived on Nantucket for about twelve years. Her interpreting work began early in the pandemic "
  "when she was asked to help translate hospital announcements for the Brazilian community; she "
  "now assists both the Brazilian and Hispanic communities daily, and was appointed to her "
  "position by a vote of the Select Board."),
]

